 "result_text": "I changed Data Format 3 detection in `ruuvitag_sensor/ruuvi.py` so it accepts the shorter payloads that RuuviFW 1.2.8 sends. I haven't run the tests or tried it against real tag data.\n\n`_get_data_format_3` used to reject any payload that wasn't exactly 54 hex characters. Firmware 1.2.8 trims trailing NULLs, so valid payloads were being rejected. It now accepts anything from 18 up to 54 characters that has the format marker `03` in the right place. It then pads the data part with `0` characters back to its full length before returning it, so the decoder gets the fixed-size input it expects.\n\nIf the firmware trims bytes that hold real data, such as the battery value, the padding will read them as zeros. I didn't change anything for #29, since the issue only describes the 1.2.8 breakage.",
